  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$(6-9\\,\\text{i})(6+9\\,\\text{i})=$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying two complex numbers is similar to multiplying two binomials. We also use the fact that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6-9\\,\\text{i})(6+9\\,\\text{i}) & =6\\cdot 6+6\\cdot 9\\,\\text{i}+(-9\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 6+(-9\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 9\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =36+54\\,\\text{i}-54\\,\\text{i}-81\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =36-81\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =36+81 \\\\  & =117.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
